{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815906-downplaying-clan-stereotype","id":815906,"title":"Downplaying Clan Stereotype","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-24T22:35:36-08:00","id":815906,"title":"Downplaying Clan Stereotype","content":"Hi there!<br /> <br /> I am starting a new chronicle soon, and I have been toying with the idea of downplaying Clan stereotypes in my games, especially since a couple of players are coming from Masquerade, so I want to offer something new. Here is what I have been thinking about doing:<br /> <br /> <b>1. Keeping only the signature discipline of each clan (Ventrue get Dominate, Mekhet keep Auspex, Daeva keep Majesty and so on).</b><br /> <br /> The second discipline would be one which meshes well with the characters' background (maybe there's a side to the character that gets even more formidable after the Embrace, or perhaps a weakling finds himself with a major change in having Vigor to fight back when a bully approaches!)<br /> <br /> The third one would be a physical discipline. The way I see it, this would better help players in creating unique characters.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, Clans work TOO well as stereotypes, and I believe everybody has seen enough hardy-shapechangers Gangrel, seductive and exceedingly good in fights as Daeva, ninja-like Mekhet, and the list goes on. I wouldn't allow players to choose a signature discipline of a different clan at first. Those could be learnt as a result of their interactions with characters from different clans. <br /> <br /> <b>2. Changing some names to make things more unique</b>. The Ventrue should go, giving way to the Ven or Julii. Nosferatu is good enough to remain. As for the Gangrel, I feel like there could be a change, but I don't know which would be the best.<br /> <br /> I wonder what you think of it, and what your suggestions could be like.<br /> <br /> Thanks :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/808-tempus","name":"Tempus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T22:48:01-08:00","id":815909,"title":"","content":"But they don't force you into those stereotypes, though. Everything you're looking to break away from is strictly narrative; I've had a Gangrel scientist who was terrified of his &quot;panic attacks&quot; and could easily see a Ventrue that is a crazy recluse can't get along with human beings but loves his animal friends. Your Mekhet can be a twitchy kung fu-obsessed nutjob with Tertiary Mental attributes that doesn't know shit about the occult and a Daeva that doesn't give a shit about being an object of sexual desire (and is terrified of it).<br /> <br /> I do agree with point 2, though. As for names, I go for Lords (Ventrue), Worms (Nosferatu), Fiends (Daeva), Shades (Mekhet), and Mongrels (Gangrel). Thank Danse Macabre for those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T23:14:24-08:00","id":815919,"title":"","content":"1. Considering you don't choose your clan in-character and that your clan's sterotype might not fit your character at all, I don't feel that it is necessary.<br /> 2. I'd use the nicknames from 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T23:21:38-08:00","id":815922,"title":"","content":"Thank you for sharing your opinion!<br /> <br /> To be honest, I am perfectly fine with making sure my characters are not one dimensional, However, I feel that the vast majority of players are still too concerned about the Disciplines and the fluff before thinking about a unique character. Most of them come up with nice stories and good backgrounds, but at the end of the day they will still resort to dominating minds and commanding animals, seducing and fighting, being fast and unseen while seeing a lot, shapeshifting and using crazy details and ditching subtlety almost entirely and so on. That is what I am trying to avoid. Players tend, and rightfully so, to rely on their supernatural powers. It sounds like a good idea to have 2 Gangrel with some of the fluff in common, but different disciplines to achieve their goals and full-fill their desired roles from the start. It makes it more personal. In my opinion, that is!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/808-tempus","name":"Tempus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T00:10:53-08:00","id":815934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tempus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815906-downplaying-clan-stereotype?p=815922#post815922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for sharing your opinion!<br /> <br /> To be honest, I am perfectly fine with making sure my characters are not one dimensional, However, I feel that the vast majority of players are still too concerned about the Disciplines and the fluff before thinking about a unique character. Most of them come up with nice stories and good backgrounds, but at the end of the day they will still resort to dominating minds and commanding animals, seducing and fighting, being fast and unseen while seeing a lot, shapeshifting and using crazy details and ditching subtlety almost entirely and so on. That is what I am trying to avoid. Players tend, and rightfully so, to rely on their supernatural powers. It sounds like a good idea to have 2 Gangrel with some of the fluff in common, but different disciplines to achieve their goals and full-fill their desired roles from the start. It makes it more personal. In my opinion, that is!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But this changes nothing... your players will still do &quot;dominating minds and commanding animals, seducing and fighting, being fast and unseen while seeing a lot, shapeshifting and using crazy details and ditching subtlety almost entirely and so on&quot;, just with different powers. This has nothing to do with clan stereotypes... This has to do with good old &quot;we're playing monsters&quot; if you want to see less power usage you need to play something which.. well, uses less powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T05:35:10-08:00","id":816032,"title":"","content":"Clan stereotypes in Requiem are pretty much opt-in as it is. Clan gives you 1) pick of two favored attribute, 2) affinity powers that anyone can still purchase, 3) optional merits, and 4) clan banes that are pretty easy to all but ignore as is. What's new from Masquerade is that clans dont' really shape your personality, goals, drives, or anything like that. That's what covenant is for. All clan does is give you a few bonuses. Genetics gives you some leanings in life, but ultimately doesn't determine who you are - your upbringing and decisions have a significant role in that.<br /> <br /> And I agree with Griautis. If your problem is the players falling back on Disciplines, this has nothing to do with clan stereotypes and everything to do with the players wanting to use their shiny magic powers. Its a playstyle where you're going to have to hack the powers themselves, or play up the drawbacks of using them, if you want a change. Whcih might not be welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T05:37:30-08:00","id":816033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815906-downplaying-clan-stereotype?p=815934#post815934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But this changes nothing... your players will still [...] <b>just with different powers</b>. This has nothing to do with clan stereotypes... This has to do with good old &quot;we're playing monsters&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly the point. I believe it would add a bit more flavour to their characters other than 'this is the kit my clan can give me, and this is the stereotype I'm well-equipped with by default'.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/808-tempus","name":"Tempus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T05:43:23-08:00","id":816036,"title":"","content":"Well then... just drop the idea of clans altogether? Have a single pool of disciplines to choose from and be done with it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You can use a bane akin to Mekhet - choose your own Unique Bane, as if taking oen up for Breaking Point removal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T06:20:15-08:00","id":816048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815906-downplaying-clan-stereotype?p=816032#post816032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clan stereotypes in Requiem are pretty much opt-in as it is. Clan gives you 1) pick of two favored attribute, 2) affinity powers that anyone can still purchase, 3) optional merits, and 4) clan banes that are pretty easy to all but ignore as is. What's new from Masquerade is that clans dont' really shape your personality, goals, drives, or anything like that. That's what covenant is for. All clan does is give you a few bonuses. Genetics gives you some leanings in life, but ultimately doesn't determine who you are - your upbringing and decisions have a significant role in that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the flavour the clans can add. What I want to change this time round is to have the characters' personality shape their powers a bit more. As it is now, clan disciplines are like a 'kit', and it can be rather limiting, especially to newer players. For instance, I like the idea of the enigmatic, shadowy vampire who uncovers secrets. As it is now, a player is likely to pick clan Mekhet because of disciplines available. If the only 'mandatory power' available by selecting this clan were AUSPEX, then such player could think a bit better: maybe DOMINATE could help me achieve the same goal, but differently? Maybe a Gangrel with both PROTEAN and OBFUSCATE could reach places unavailable to most? What about a Daeva who can influence somebody's emotions with MAJESTY, and still have ANIMALISM to make sure he can monitor his targets more easily without being discovered?<br /> <br /> It is a way to allow players to pick and choose. The clan flavour is still there, but the 'kit' is a lot less important by default, and things such as 'I want a fighter type, I'm DEFINITELY picking a Daeva because of the in-clan disciplines' (regardless of how poor such a mindset is in the game) would not be so black and white. Perhaps the same character could pick a Ventrue, adding 2 physical disciplines and be able to accomplish the same, but differently. I know that a lot of that is possible as is, but having stereotypes and kits be less important and encourage players to deviate from the normal and tired splats (no matter how flavourful their backstories are) is my goal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815906-downplaying-clan-stereotype?p=816032#post816032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your problem is the players falling back on Disciplines, this has nothing to do with clan stereotypes and everything to do with the players wanting to use their shiny magic powers. Its a playstyle where you're going to have to hack the powers themselves, or play up the drawbacks of using them, if you want a change. Whcih might not be welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am completely fine with all kinds of characters. I don't want them to be less powerful. What I am looking for is giving them more of a choice, make it more personal with characters' traits and background influencing the kind of powers they can have. One power is in their blood, it runs more strongly in their veins. The others are more personal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/808-tempus","name":"Tempus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T06:33:05-08:00","id":816053,"title":"","content":"I just don't see it... they will still pick a clan depending on their powers. And people who want a Dominate focused detective.. well, they're gonna pick Dominate anyways. <br /> <br /> Well, another change you can make, is just make all disciplines cost the same amount of XP, thus keeping some clan identity, while allowing to choose any power, depending on personality?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T06:51:02-08:00","id":816063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815906-downplaying-clan-stereotype?p=816053#post816053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't see it... they will still pick a clan depending on their powers. And people who want a Dominate focused detective.. well, they're gonna pick Dominate anyways.<br /> <br /> Well, another change you can make, is just make all disciplines cost the same amount of XP, thus keeping some clan identity, while allowing to choose any power, depending on personality?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think your suggestion is similar to what I intended. They keep the clan flavour [and the signature power], but everything else is for them to decide, encouraging them to make more unique characters and play the role they want in a more personalised way. This way clans would still matter, but their impact would be diminished as they share one baseline power, but the others are a reflection of the characters' personalities and experiences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/808-tempus","name":"Tempus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T07:02:33-08:00","id":816073,"title":"","content":"But if they're choosing their own clans, don't they already have choice? And it's not like out of clan disciplines are so much more expensive. I'm partly playing a gangrel because I don't want to be a guy who solves his problems with mind control or subtlety. I don't want to be the sneaky guy. It hasn't restricted me at all.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't get Dominate even if it could solve all my character's problems right now. So I don't feel limited at all by Clan, it's only helped me refine my character concept. Further, I did/will eventually learn Nightmare from another player character, so again, I don't feel limited by Clan at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T07:21:48-08:00","id":816082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tempus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815906-downplaying-clan-stereotype?p=816048#post816048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the flavour the clans can add. What I want to change this time round is to have the characters' personality shape their powers a bit more. As it is now, clan disciplines are like a 'kit', and it can be rather limiting, especially to newer players. For instance, I like the idea of the enigmatic, shadowy vampire who uncovers secrets. As it is now, a player is likely to pick clan Mekhet because of disciplines available.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, a player that wants an secret-seeking shadow vampire will pick the Mekhet because of the bonus to mental stats, dream-uncover-secrets merit, and the disciplines. Its kind of their entire archetype. Auspex, Celerity, and Obfuscate all lend to that archetype as well, not just Auspex.<br /> <br /> And if someone wants to use Dominate to help them do all this shadowy secret uncovering... then they just start learning Dominate? This isn't Masquerade where clan disciplines were restricted to those clans. Covenant secrets are the restricted powers. Nothing stops a Mehket from learning Dominate. Or Protean. A Gangrel can easily learn Obfucate, and nothing stops a Daeva from learning Animalism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is a way to allow players to pick and choose. The clan flavour is still there, but the 'kit' is a lot less important by default, and things such as 'I want a fighter type, I'm DEFINITELY picking a Daeva because of the in-clan disciplines' (regardless of how poor such a mindset is in the game) would not be so black and white </div> </div> </div> Actually, Daeva are the fighter types by mindset in the game. They lend themselves to the rebellous Carthian mindset, and they get access to Enfeebling Aura, which turns Majesty into a combat power. The Daeva are the signuture knights of the Invictus (Spina). So, from a lore standpoint, its a perfect fit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perhaps the same character could pick a Ventrue, adding 2 physical disciplines and be able to accomplish the same, but differently. </div> </div> </div> They already get Resilience, Dominate can be powerful in combat, Animalism is good for retainer-swarms in a fight, and Vigor isn't hard to pick up as a cross-clan ability. The Ventrue can also go Ordo and pick up Coil of the Wyrm for more ability in combat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know that a lot of that is possible as is, but having stereotypes and kits be less important and encourage players to deviate from the normal and tired splats (no matter how flavourful their backstories are) is my goal.<br /> <br /> I am completely fine with all kinds of characters. I don't want them to be less powerful. What I am looking for is giving them more of a choice, make it more personal with characters' traits and background influencing the kind of powers they can have. One power is in their blood, it runs more strongly in their veins. The others are more personal. </div> </div> </div> Maybe what you need is to start looking at bloodlines? They provide variations on clan abitlies. Or just get rid of clans entirely - the first Requiem Storyteller's Guide had an options for clanless game.<br /> <br /> Honestly, it sounds like you've got some kind of fixation on the Disciplines being the sole identifying factor of the clans. And that's something I have to raise an eyebrow at. I really have to ask - are your <i>players</i> interested in this? Do they feel hemmed in by the rules?<br /> <br /> I look at all this, and I don't see anyone locked into any stereotype. I see you wantting to turn the Ventrue into a detective or warrior. Which, okay, works, because Ven can be both. And if you're keeping the signature, then people will still pick the clans based on the same &quot;tired kit.&quot; Or do you think that a secret-finder is going to pass up the option for dream-info and Auspex together? That a warrior won't be interested in Enfeebling Aura, which requires Majesty? Or someone that likes using Nightmare won't want Obfuscate (the two are designed to work together). Or that a warrior of any clan won't be interested in Body of Will?<br /> <br /> How are you even &quot;keeping&quot; signature disciplines when they can be taken by anyone as it is anyways?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-25-2016, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T08:46:27-08:00","id":816141,"title":"","content":"Vigor, Celerity and Obfuscate at one dot each is a valid starting spread for three different clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T10:28:21-08:00","id":816231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tempus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815906-downplaying-clan-stereotype#post815906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi there!<br /> <br /> I am starting a new chronicle soon, and I have been toying with the idea of downplaying Clan stereotypes in my games, especially since a couple of players are coming from Masquerade, so I want to offer something new. Here is what I have been thinking about doing:<br /> <br /> <b>1. Keeping only the signature discipline of each clan (Ventrue get Dominate, Mekhet keep Auspex, Daeva keep Majesty and so on).</b><br /> <br /> The second discipline would be one which meshes well with the characters' background (maybe there's a side to the character that gets even more formidable after the Embrace, or perhaps a weakling finds himself with a major change in having Vigor to fight back when a bully approaches!)<br /> <br /> The third one would be a physical discipline. The way I see it, this would better help players in creating unique characters.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, Clans work TOO well as stereotypes, and I believe everybody has seen enough hardy-shapechangers Gangrel, seductive and exceedingly good in fights as Daeva, ninja-like Mekhet, and the list goes on. I wouldn't allow players to choose a signature discipline of a different clan at first. Those could be learnt as a result of their interactions with characters from different clans.<br /> <br /> <b>2. Changing some names to make things more unique</b>. The Ventrue should go, giving way to the Ven or Julii. Nosferatu is good enough to remain. As for the Gangrel, I feel like there could be a change, but I don't know which would be the best.<br /> <br /> I wonder what you think of it, and what your suggestions could be like.<br /> <br /> Thanks :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be contradicting yourself. The question is what do your players want?<br /> That is the key. They may want the clans.<br /> <br /> If you keep the clans I would suggest this, explain to them that Requiem clans are more like the proposed lineages (ventrue , tzim are from the kingly ruler line). While the requiem bloodlines are more like Masquerade clans.<br /> <br /> Also the Requiem Clan books in many cases did a good job of portraying alternate versions of the clan types. Nothing stops you from awarding an out of clan common at creation if something in the character's background warrants it. Maybe even a special if there is really a good reason. Though I'd be careful with that.<br /> <br /> While I like the Clans one thing I've thought about is Clan not being necessarily inherited. This actually easier in 2 Ed since clane bane does not kick in until Humanity 6.<br /> Gangrel can sire a Nos for example. Is it something in childes nature? Is it something in their requiem that determines it? Can some elders breed true? And if so how?<br /> Maybe they don't start out with the clan specials. Maybe picking that up sets Clan? Or Maybe something else determines Clan , Nature or Requiem, and once Clan activates the special becomes available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","user":"Chattnos","date":". 01-25-2016, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T10:30:29-08:00","id":816237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815906-downplaying-clan-stereotype?p=816082#post816082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, a player that wants an secret-seeking shadow vampire will pick the Mekhet because of the bonus to mental stats, dream-uncover-secrets merit, and the disciplines. Its kind of their entire archetype. Auspex, Celerity, and Obfuscate all lend to that archetype as well, not just Auspex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is part of what I am trying to avoid. The entire 'kit' is strong in this regard, and players are likely to follow just that, which isn't really that much different from Masquerade or the original Requiem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815906-downplaying-clan-stereotype?p=816082#post816082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if someone wants to use Dominate to help them do all this shadowy secret uncovering... then they just start learning Dominate? This isn't Masquerade where clan disciplines were restricted to those clans. Covenant secrets are the restricted powers. Nothing stops a Mehket from learning Dominate. Or Protean. A Gangrel can easily learn Obfucate, and nothing stops a Daeva from learning Animalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that still means clan powers take precedence over the character's traits. The fact of the matter is that it's interesting to have some of the power reflect what the character is, not that 'okay, you're now a Daeva, so you have a supernatural affinity to being stronger, faster and more charming, despite the fact that you've been a geeky librarian all your life who doesn't really care too much about social interaction, exercising or whatever. You're still a Daeva, but none of the powers suit you well. They can be useful, but they won't suit the character. Plus, the very thing about 'the clan chooses you' in a way is just helping make stereotypes stronger.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815906-downplaying-clan-stereotype?p=816082#post816082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, Daeva are the fighter types by mindset in the game. They lend themselves to the rebellous Carthian mindset, and they get access to Enfeebling Aura, which turns Majesty into a combat power. The Daeva are the signuture knights of the Invictus (Spina). So, from a lore standpoint, its a perfect fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they? They are the signature knights of the Invictus because of their disciplines. It makes them fit the archetype more easily. That is another thing I am trying to avoid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815906-downplaying-clan-stereotype?p=816082#post816082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They already get Resilience, Dominate can be powerful in combat, Animalism is good for retainer-swarms in a fight, and Vigor isn't hard to pick up as a cross-clan ability. The Ventrue can also go Ordo and pick up Coil of the Wyrm for more ability in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that is exactly the situation I'm trying to avoid. 'A Ventrue can fight like this', 'a Daeva will fight like that', 'a Gangrel will do this and that'. That is only the case because of the powers available to them. And it is the very thing I'm trying to keep away from. <br /> <br /> It is not a matter of 'so I pick this clan because it usually plays like this'. It is more along the lines of 'I like the mood, I like the tone, I like the role, but if I love the Gangrel fluff and I want to have a character that can be better at mental powers. Going by the rules as they are, a Gangrel wouldn't be good at that from the get go. It wouldn't reflect the character's personality or background. But the character would be stuck with Reslience and Animalism despite not being interested in those in the slightest. Or, worse yet, the player would be more inclined to choose a DIFFERENT CLAN just because of the powers alone. Of course players can get out of clan disciplines, join a bloodline or something similar, but that still means that the character's personality has very little impact on their 'curse'.<br /> <br /> As for bloodlines and covenant books, we are staying away from those from the time being. Most of the group is new to Requiem, but half the players are familiar with the Masquerade, and they don't want clans dictation too much.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the opinions, loving it so far. It always adds a new perspective which I hadn't considered. Gotta love it! :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/808-tempus","name":"Tempus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T10:38:55-08:00","id":816245,"title":"","content":"&quot;You used to be a geeky librarian who didn't work out much. Now you're now a geeky librarian who still doesn't work out much but can somehow bench press a motorcycle.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T11:09:02-08:00","id":816275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815906-downplaying-clan-stereotype?p=816245#post816245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;You used to be a geeky librarian who didn't work out much. Now you're now a geeky librarian who still doesn't work out much but can somehow bench press a motorcycle.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Which, while very cool in itself, might be something that the player isn't terribly interested in. What if such geeky librarian could, instead, bench press that motorcycle, being charmer than he could ever have imagined and... still get Auspex because it's part of his nature, or Obfuscate because he's used to hiding away, or even Animalism due to his being closer to animals, maybe training them, perhaps preferring their company?<br /> <br /> That could become core to this character without having to think about other in or out of clan disciplines right from the start. That is the thing; A character can eventually become something entirely different, learn new disciplines and other cool powers... But maybe, just maybe, the person the character was before could dictate a bit more, and the Daeva wouldn't be 'prince charming who's also great combat', but something more, more unique, and if that could be true for this character, the entirety of the clan would feel a lot less defined as well :-D<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815906-downplaying-clan-stereotype?p=816231#post816231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to be contradicting yourself. The question is what do your players want?<br /> That is the key. They may want the clans</div> </div> </div> </div>They want the clans. They want them to be a bit different. The change in some of the names is important because some players are coming from Masquerade, and we feel that repeating some of the same names isn't particularly useful. That's okay.<br /> <br /> As for the clans, after they read the fluff for each clan their opinions were very stereotypical. One of them loved the fluff behind the Mekhet, but he doesn't like Obfuscate and Celerity. Of course he could get out of clan disciplines... He was more interested in the disciplines the Gangrel have, but the fluff didn't sit well with him. His ideal character would probably have Auspex, Resilience and Animalism for disciplines. I told him that maybe the Ventrue with the added Auspex could be a nice fit. He, again, wasn't interested in playing a 'megalomaniac'. LOL. At first I would think 'that is being picky', but then I realised that allowing them to have the fluff, a base core power which is normal to the entire lineage and allow them to choose whatever other powers they like as a reflection of their characters and the roles they want to play would be a lot simpler than going through bloodlines, in and out of clan disciplines, allowing him to pick an extra one to be his in-clan power when he simply wasn't interested in the other two powers to begin with<br /> <br /> This way they could keep the fluff, keep a core power for the entire clan and still have a lot of room for personalisation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/808-tempus","user":"Tempus","date":". 01-25-2016, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/808-tempus","name":"Tempus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T11:24:23-08:00","id":816285,"title":"","content":"You do know a daeva can learn auspex or animalism or obfuscate if they want, right?<br /> <br /> Ok, nevermind, you edited it after I started typing. But still, the answer to &quot;but I don't want to play a megalomaniac&quot; is &quot;Well fucking don't then&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 01-25-2016, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T12:12:30-08:00","id":816330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tempus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815906-downplaying-clan-stereotype?p=816237#post816237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is part of what I am trying to avoid. The entire 'kit' is strong in this regard, and players are likely to follow just that, which isn't really that much different from Masquerade or the original Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div> You miss my point. You're hyper/laser focused on Disciplines to the point you're missing forest for the trees. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But that still means clan powers take precedence over the character's traits. The fact of the matter is that it's interesting to have some of the power reflect what the character is, not that 'okay, you're now a Daeva, so you have a supernatural affinity to being stronger, faster and more charming, despite the fact that you've been a geeky librarian all your life who doesn't really care too much about social interaction, exercising or whatever. You're still a Daeva, but none of the powers suit you well. They can be useful, but they won't suit the character. Plus, the very thing about 'the clan chooses you' in a way is just helping make stereotypes stronger. </div> </div> </div> No one is forcing you to learn any of the clan affinity disciplines. You need to start with two dots worth of magical powers, then you learn a third from anywhere. Hell, as a geeky librarian turned Daeva, the Lancea Sanctum or Ordo Dracul would love to have you in their ranks to help with studies and their magics.<br /> <br /> Plus, you also get some Dex or Manipulation. The Embrace DOES change someone on a fundamental level. You have a new set of &quot;genetics&quot; that help shape who you are now. <br /> <br /> Then, there's the question about -why-. Why was the anti-social geeky librarian embraced by a succubus in the first place, when its such an ill fit? Sounds like a kick ass story hook to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are they? They are the signature knights of the Invictus because of their disciplines. </div> </div> </div> Nooooooo.... they're the signature knights of the Invictus because they were the first knightly bloodline created that would fit the &quot;passion&quot; of knightly pride with the 1e daeva weakness, and they grew to be awesomely popular. Has nothing to do with the baseline Daeva Disciplines. If any &quot;discipline&quot; is to blame, it would be Courtise, the bloodline specific discipline, which has no bearing on this discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that is exactly the situation I'm trying to avoid. </div> </div> </div> Except its a generic situation. Any vampire combatant is going to focus on Vigor and Resilience. Anyone can do retainer swarms. You're not really changing anything, because, frankly, the number of &quot;fighting possibilities&quot; is pretty small in the first place for a vampire. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is not a matter of 'so I pick this clan because it usually plays like this'. It is more along the lines of 'I like the mood, I like the tone, I like the role, but if I love the Gangrel fluff and I want to have a character that can be better at mental powers. Going by the rules as they are, a Gangrel wouldn't be good at that from the get go. It wouldn't reflect the character's personality or background. </div> </div> </div> A few things. One - <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-jaws-of-the-beast/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/the-jaws-of-the-beast/</a><br /> <br /> And two - I read your quote as, &quot;I like the mood of being an unstopable animalistic vampire. But I don't want to take any powers that make me unstopable or animalistic.&quot; Seriously. I'm really having a very hard time believing someone is goign to be in love with the story and tone and feeling of the Gangrel, but hating Animalism and Resilience. Especially when they can just invest their two dots in Protean, one in another discipline, and then join a covenant.<br /> <br /> Three - So what? It doesn't match your character's personality or background? <i>That's what happens</i>. You don't choose your family is a theme in the game for a reason. And the only time someone is going to choose mismatched concepts like that is if they're doing it deliberately for a character. Maybe they want to struggle between their new inhuman body and their old human life. <br /> Four - Circle of the Crone has a very Gangrel mindset to it as a whole. Just like the Invictus feel very Ventrue-ish, and the Ordo has a Mehket-y mindset, etc. There's a reason we have covenants as the family you choose.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or, worse yet, the player would be more inclined to choose a DIFFERENT CLAN just because of the powers alone. </div> </div> </div> So? You don't think that there are Ventrue and Daeva who join the Ordo Dracul because they're more interested in mystical explroation of the self than socializing or fighting? That's part of the raison d'etre of covenants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course players can get out of clan disciplines, join a bloodline or something similar, but that still means that the character's personality has very little impact on their 'curse'. </div> </div> </div> Yeah, kind of the point. You don't choose yoru family is a theme in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for bloodlines and covenant books, we are staying away from those from the time being. Most of the group is new to Requiem, but half the players are familiar with the Masquerade, and they don't want clans dictation too much. </div> </div> </div> Clan isn't dictating anything. Covenant does. In Masquerade, clan determined your thought processes, how you felt or believed. In Requiem, clan just gives you a genetic inclination, like a fast or slow metabolism. And you join a Covenant that you agree with philosphically. There's no diction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T12:34:28-08:00","id":816346,"title":"","content":"Looks to me like you're carrying shitloads of bagagge here from Masquarade.. the only way I can see it. Because otherwise, you're fighting the Clan makeups of disciplinessaying their forcing too much on it, but you don't want to ditch them too? <br /> <br /> Seriously, just allow them to pick any disciplines... I'll bet you'll see your players picking the clan powers without being forced to anyways. When you want to play a stealth character, you will pickobfuscate.. same for investigatory and auspex.. andif we keep to the fluff at least a bit, they'll pick Mekhet too for that intelligence/wits bonus (for investigator...)<br /> <br /> Your two desires seem at cross points. One of them will have to give in (either the desire to have Clans still bring flavor.. or clans, for a true pick what you are yourself experience). Otherwise the players will pick the clans most fitting to their characters... (or deliberately not, to play against those stereotypes)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T13:40:06-08:00","id":816399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tempus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815906-downplaying-clan-stereotype?p=816237#post816237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that still means clan powers take precedence over the character's traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dice pool does include skills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tempus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815906-downplaying-clan-stereotype?p=816275#post816275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which, while very cool in itself, might be something that the player isn't terribly interested in. What if such geeky librarian could, instead, bench press that motorcycle, being charmer than he could ever have imagined and... still get Auspex because it's part of his nature, or Obfuscate because he's used to hiding away, or even Animalism due to his being closer to animals, maybe training them, perhaps preferring their company?<br /> <br /> That could become core to this character without having to think about other in or out of clan disciplines right from the start. That is the thing; A character can eventually become something entirely different, learn new disciplines and other cool powers... But maybe, just maybe, the person the character was before could dictate a bit more, and the Daeva wouldn't be 'prince charming who's also great combat', but something more, more unique, and if that could be true for this character, the entirety of the clan would feel a lot less defined as well :-D<br /> <br /> They want the clans. They want them to be a bit different. The change in some of the names is important because some players are coming from Masquerade, and we feel that repeating some of the same names isn't particularly useful. That's okay.<br /> <br /> As for the clans, after they read the fluff for each clan their opinions were very stereotypical. One of them loved the fluff behind the Mekhet, but he doesn't like Obfuscate and Celerity. Of course he could get out of clan disciplines... He was more interested in the disciplines the Gangrel have, but the fluff didn't sit well with him. His ideal character would probably have Auspex, Resilience and Animalism for disciplines. I told him that maybe the Ventrue with the added Auspex could be a nice fit. He, again, wasn't interested in playing a 'megalomaniac'. LOL. At first I would think 'that is being picky', but then I realised that allowing them to have the fluff, a base core power which is normal to the entire lineage and allow them to choose whatever other powers they like as a reflection of their characters and the roles they want to play would be a lot simpler than going through bloodlines, in and out of clan disciplines, allowing him to pick an extra one to be his in-clan power when he simply wasn't interested in the other two powers to begin with<br /> <br /> This way they could keep the fluff, keep a core power for the entire clan and still have a lot of room for personalisation.</div> </div> </div> </div>First are you playing first edition or second?<br /> Second allows for other clans besides the 5. You could write up your own. <br /> On name changes I call the Nos Neferatu, which is transilvanian for demon or afflicted.<br /> <br /> Blood and smoke is about trasitioning perhap your mehkhet who wants animalism is on his way to create a bloodlineor a member thereof.<br /> <br /> You could let pick a signature discpline and then take just the bane but to me the clan don't seem like clans anymore.<br /> Just let go clanless and let them pick discplines and banes as they see fit.<br /> PS I HATE THIS GD WORDPRESS FORUM THAT DOESN&quot;T LET YOU EDIT.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T13:45:59-08:00","id":816406,"title":"","content":"I think a Ventrue who deliberately never touches Dominate because they don't like the idea of taking someone's free will would be a very interesting character to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T15:15:14-08:00","id":816458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815906-downplaying-clan-stereotype?p=816406#post816406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a Ventrue who deliberately never touches Dominate because they don't like the idea of taking someone's free will would be a very interesting character to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. And let us not forget the Ventrue are not quite the same as Masq ventrue. At first blush they are but they are more than that. And many ways more distant and alien than old Masq ventrue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T07:27:10-08:00","id":816858,"title":"","content":"OP - A mechanical suggestion for what you maybe want (avoiding the why you might want it).<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Players Choose a Clan. They take the Bane of that Clan, and choose one of the Clan's three disciplines to cost 3 XP per dot (i.e. - In-Clan).</li> <li>Players choose two other disciplines of the basic 10, they then cost 3 XP per dot as above.</li> </ol>Alternative (weird) system:<ul><li>All disciplines costs 3 xp per dot. Any character that takes a signature discipline from a Clan (Auspex, Dominate, Majesty, Nightmare, Protean) also gets that Clan's bane. They can take multiple signature disciplines at the cost of another bane. If you want to force scarcity, count this against the &quot;three optional banes&quot; limit per character.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T07:47:35-08:00","id":816872,"title":"","content":"You want to do away with clan stereotypes, then don't use the pregenerated NPCs in the books and don't tack them onto your own created NPCs. The local brothel owner isn't a silicon Daeva with Majesty cranked up to the max 24/7 and their retinue of blood addicted Vigor enhanced bouncers. It's actually a cross dressing (insert ANY other clan here) who mixes level 5 of Obfuscate to create ambiance and level 5 of Animalism for their by invitation only guests' security.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T15:36:22-08:00","id":819541,"title":"","content":"It's really easy to break Clan Stereotype in Requiem.<br /> <br /> I'm playing a Mekhet Man In Black working as an Invictus Knight.<br /> <br /> One of my friends is playing... Caspar, the greatest mastermind and socialite in the city. <br /> He's a Nosferatu.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T16:15:12-08:00","id":819565,"title":"","content":"It helps that Nosferatu's shtick in Requiem is &quot;Fucking Terrifying&quot; and not &quot;ugly sewer-dweller&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T08:42:58-08:00","id":819814,"title":"","content":"Clans don't inform who you are, but how you act. They're methods of being a vampire, and each one has more than one methodology. The one thing I advise is to not dismiss how Clan can affect a person's worldview entirely. It's not a matter of a &quot;culture&quot; per say, but how do you view people when you just don't really feel attached to even the most important people in your life (Ventrue curse), you can look people in the eyes and tell them what to do (Dominate), animals yield to you (Animalism) and people that try to hurt you just find that you shrug it off (Resilience)<br /> <br /> Your disciplines and your clan bane give strong behavioral cues for characters. How they react to it will vary from person to person, but the one commonality between members of different clans is that they will experience those same stimuli. Maybe even react to it the same way. Those Kindred uniquely understand the perks and stressors of <i>your </i>existence, which is one reason why you might come together as it were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T17:49:26-08:00","id":820054,"title":"","content":"Sorry for taking so long to reply to this. Busy week at work!<br /> <br /> Many great opinions, and that's exactly what I was looking for.<br /> <br /> In the end, the players decided to do away with the clans. They were a lot more interested in the covenants. They created some bizarre characters. One got Auspex, Animalism and Resilience, strong mental attributes and skills. He was very interested in being Carthian for some reason. The other got a really crazy monster with all three physical disciplines and high mental attributes and skills. According to the player, that's a manifestation in a character who once was weak in life but feels stronger and confident in death... He didn't pick physical skills because he said his character lacked such training. He went with Lancea, deciding that his character could very well be the punishment from heavens. Interesting. The last one decided to go for a very domineering character with high mental and physical capabilities, including Dominate, Vigor and Cruac.<br /> <br /> Everybody is happy.<br /> <br /> If there are any more ideas or comments, they will be great to know. <br /> <br /> Thanks a lot! =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/808-tempus","name":"Tempus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T11:47:53-08:00","id":820470,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised that 2e didn't include Clanless vampires as an optional rule in the corebook, considering it has a couple suggestions that either don't fit the game style people around here play (Above All Else Feed and the one that replaces Attributes with Mask and Dirge come to mind), or even one which is a variant of 'award more XP' (Blood Beats). A Clanless/Covenantless game would focus the game more on 'the family you choose' or 'the family you are stuck with' respectively.<br /> <br /> For the record, if you're going Clanless, I recommend pricing all Disciplines at 4XP/dot and then bumping up the Beats/Experiences you award. Entirely because Resilience and Vigor are literally better than Strength and Stamina in every way, and being cheaper than the Attributes just means nobody is ever going to raise mundane Strength until they have 5 Vigor (even at 4XP/dot people will be doing this, but it's the standard cost for Out-of-Clans now).<br /> <br /> Oh, and for the record, Bloodlines aren't hard, they essentially amount to a little bit of backstory, an extra discipline, a bane, and possibly swapping out a Clan Discipline. For example, if a player wants a psychic-focused Gangrel they might have the following as part of their bloodline:<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Animalism, Auspex, Dominate, Protean (In all seriousness, think very carefully before giving a bloodline 3 signature disciplines, getting ones outside of your clan is supposed to be hard and requires a 1st stage Blood Bond for the first dot)<br /> <b>Bloodline Bane:</b> through interacting with civilised minds, the mind of the [bloodline] has become more detached from humanity. You no longer gain a bonus to detachment rolls from having an attached touchstone. (Holy Vampires Batman, this is a horrible weakness! I just had few ideas)<br /> <br /> But you don't need a bloodline to stuff a concept into a clan. Let's look at the Daeva geeky librarian:<br /> -Celerity I can see, if the librarian is known for being very efficient. Maybe a point or two here.<br /> -Majesty I can see them maybe having a point here, but I can't articulate why.<br /> -Vigor I can definitely see them having points in. They've read the stories, they expect Vampires to be strong, and it's in-clan so they can learn it without a teacher.<br /> -The Clan Bane I have a sight problem with, but I can see them creating a herd of 'close friends' to feed on.<br /> So for a Daeva Librarian I'd suggest the following starting discipline spread:<br /> -Celerity 1<br /> -Obfucscate 1<br /> -Vigor 1<br /> <br /> Now remember, you can take a concept and apply it to different Clans, for example, a Prince interpreted as the stereotype of four of the five clans.<br /> -<b>Daeva:</b> the charismatic leader.<br /> -<b>Mekhet:</b> the scholar-king, leading with wise decisions but not personality.<br /> -<b>Nosferatu:</b> the ruler-through fear.<br /> -<b>Ventrue: </b>ruling with an iron fist, the aristocratic ruler...<br /> I can't think of an example for the Gangrel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T13:11:12-08:00","id":820531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815906-downplaying-clan-stereotype?p=820470#post820470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised that 2e didn't include Clanless vampires as an optional rule in the corebook, considering it has a couple suggestions that either don't fit the game style people around here play (Above All Else Feed and the one that replaces Attributes with Mask and Dirge come to mind), or even one which is a variant of 'award more XP' (Blood Beats). A Clanless/Covenantless game would focus the game more on 'the family you choose' or 'the family you are stuck with' respectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Revenants are the clanless vampires of VtR, it seems.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T13:16:55-08:00","id":820534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815906-downplaying-clan-stereotype?p=820531#post820531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revenants are the clanless vampires of VtR, it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I didn't mean Clanless as in Masquerade's Caitiff, I meant Clanless as in the entire game is Clanless. Sure, it's easy to do, throw out the idea of In-Clans and have everybody take a bane when they first fall to humanity 6, but that's why I'm surprised it wasn't given as an option in the Storytelling chapter in a section about manipulating themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T14:53:11-08:00","id":820576,"title":"","content":"The core book was about Vampire the Requiem and its setting. Options to play with other settings that throw away Vampire the Requiem stuff would likely be in a Chronicler's Guide or book of alternate rules like Danse Macabre. For instance a guide on playing the game without clans is in chapter two of the Vampire the Requiem Chronicler's Guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T15:05:43-08:00","id":820583,"title":"","content":"I see a few ways of going &quot;Clanless&quot;, if one is inclined to do so. You could let players chose any 3 Disciplines to be &quot;in-Clan&quot;, as the OP has done, possibly with restrictions on which ones you can select (like &quot;at least one common and no more than one rare discipline&quot; or some such). Alternatively, you could charge either 3 or 4 experience for all Disciplines and do away with the idea of Discipline affinity alltogether. Either way, you'd have to let the players chose one of the five Clan Banes and an Attribute to favor.<br /> <br /> Another way to do it might be to keep the Clan packages intact, but make them archetypes rather than families. Everyone is still either a sexy vampire, an animalistic vampire, a sneaky vampire, a spooky vampire, or a noble vampire, but your sire's archetype has no bearing on what your archetype will be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}